title The record nobody proved -- the order record, read whole
prompt baton lap; patchouli lane; the card's own YOURS ask from my last lap, whether a whole-record comparison belongs beside every published record type
rota lap 5361, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; feel for the seam by pressing it, so the lap pressed the record's lift and lower rather than reasoning about which record types owe a comparison
think Reds first: the three OPEN rows touching this lane all want Keaton's word -- %807 names three doors for the head insert, %767 changes what the product admits, %765 is a 41-family molt. So the constructive queue was the card's own ask.
think Answering the ask by measuring the population rather than ruling on it. grep says to_order_record and from_order_record are read by mantra/src/weave.rye and mantra/src/main.rye and by no witness, while the rostered mantra_weave_v2 proves the ELDER record's pair from both sides. The ask named a policy question and the measurement named a hole.
think Three readings do stand over the newer record and each is blind to one thing: mantra_cli_record asserts the header and the row's field COUNT, mantra_document_roundtrip compares rendered document text. A writer and a reader agreeing on arity and disagreeing on assignment keeps six fields and renders an identical document where site is constant zero.
think The comparison is written ONCE and generic over the row type rather than per record type, since 23 copies of one rule is exactly what grass and pheromone are sweeping out of glow/ this hour. A field type it does not state reaches a compileError naming it.
obs The pen caught my own coverage gap. The lower_ord plant -- a lowering writing a position where the order key belongs, the exact fault %680 was opened for -- exited 0, because every weave my first draft built carried ord == pos and no claim could tell the order key from the position. Claim 5 builds a REPLACEMENT and asserts at least one row's order key stands apart from its position; the plant now exits 134.
obs The measurement that says the repair matters is a leg rather than a sentence. Planting the site-run swap once and running it under three witnesses: this guard refuses, and mantra_weave_merge and mantra_weave_apply both still reach GREEN. Asserted as blindness_held=yes, since a blindness claim left unasserted is prose.
obs Two prefix-matchable readings caught in my own runner before it shipped: contains "lift_swap_exit=1" welcomes lift_swap_exit=134. The control prints centrepiece_caught, blindness_held and count_wall_caught as WORDS now, because a word cannot be half-matched.
obs One repair rode along on touch: mantra_cli_record asserted row_fields=6 under a message reading "five fields", stale since the order key landed. Walled now against mantra/src/weave.rye's published order_row_fields, and proven to red by moving the constant to 5 and back.
obs The cold endurance run read three reds, none in this lane: seed_link (copal's live claim), fold_shelf_link_repoint, vocabulary_collection. Named rather than swept.
obs THE HOT ENDURANCE RUN DID NOT COMPLETE, and the shortfall is named rather than claimed. It read 15 guards with zero reds and then stalled past ten minutes on a glow-family guard; the pier's eight ships contend and a hot pass rebuilds where the cold one reads warm caches, so the cold pass took 91 guards in 25 minutes and the hot took 15 in 45. A scoped hot pass would have been the right instrument and it refuses here: the run header reads roster_receipt=miss, and a scoped pass chains only from a full green. So this lap's proof is the 15 hot guards, the 91 cold ones, and every witness in this lane run GREEN on metal against the staged bytes -- more than a claim, less than item 7 asks, and said plainly.
obs Inherited and unmoved: mantra/src/weave.rye reads C+/78 at Field, reach=50 on a 121-line head with 108 living citers and meter_shadow 98. Graded before and after from its committed bytes -- identical, so this lap moved nothing there and a head molt is its own lap.
